Krita Nova 64 - Autosave to the documents' own files

Settings > Configure Krita > General > File Handling gets "Save Documents
to Their Own Files Automatically" (off by default) with "Save every: N min"
(1-240, default 10), under Krita's own "Enable Autosaving", which stays as
it is (a backup copy for crash recovery).

When on, every N minutes KisNovaFileAutoSaver (created by KisPart) saves
each open document that has unsaved changes over its own file, as File >
Save does, without dialogs (the format's last export settings are used).
Only documents that already have a file in a format that keeps layers
(.kra, .psd, .ora) are saved; new unsaved images, recovered documents and
other formats (e.g. .png, .jpg - saving would flatten them) are left to the
backup autosave. A document that is being saved or whose image is busy is
tried again 30 s later. kritarc: novaAutoSaveToFile,
novaAutoSaveToFileInterval (minutes).

